    <!-- User Guide & WorldTour Science -->
    <string name="title_guide_config">How to Configure on Hammerhead Karoo</string>
    <string name="guide_step1">1. Open any Ride Profile in Karoo device settings.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2">2. Edit your data screens and choose an empty layout slot.</string>
    <string name="guide_step3">3. Under the \'Karoo BBrakers\' section, select any numerical or graphical field.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4">4. Telemetry is saved into your FIT files for Strava &amp; Intervals.icu review.</string>

    <string name="title_guide_science">WorldTour Braking Physics &amp; Science</string>
    <string name="science_topic1_title">1. Dynamic Load Transfer &amp; Front Bias</string>
    <string name="science_topic1_desc">Under hard braking, inertial force transfers up to 85% of normal load to the front contact patch. Downhill slope further increases front load. The algorithm dynamically calculates front/rear bias in real time.</string>
    <string name="science_topic2_title">2. Kamm\'s Friction Circle &amp; Washout Prevention</string>
    <string name="science_topic2_desc">A tire has a finite adhesion limit (μ·N). Combined longitudinal braking and lateral cornering forces must not exceed this limit: a_comb = √(a_x² + a_y²) ≤ μ·g. Our grip margin monitor protects against catastrophic front wheel washout.</string>
    <string name="science_topic3_title">3. Dual Thermodynamics &amp; Carbon Rim Fade</string>
    <string name="science_topic3_desc">Front calipers experience clean oncoming laminar airflow (higher heat transfer coefficient h), while rear calipers are shielded in turbulent chainstay air. Carbon rim tracks cannot exceed 180°C without risking resin delamination.</string>
    <string name="science_topic4_title">4. Peloton Feathering &amp; Involuntary Drag</string>
    <string name="science_topic4_desc">Riding in pacelines requires subtle rear brake feathering to trim distance without disrupting the group. The extension isolates feathering from emergency stops and continuously detects parasitic brake rubbing (Wasted Watts).</string>

